; `.axbad` because it must NOT compile. An `extern` naming a symbol no
; archive defines is AX4004, refused before `opt` or `cc` runs.
;
; This is the probe that tells the FFI apart from the `foreign` it
; replaced. `foreign` emitted a call to an undeclared symbol, passed
; `check`, and died two stages later inside `opt` with a message about
; generated code. The gate requires AX4004 AND requires the strings
; `opt:` and `AX4003` to be absent: a refusal arriving from the native
; toolchain is the old bug wearing a new name.
(pub extern "axiom_demo"
  (noSuchThing :: (-> Int Int) (symbol "axffi_no_such_thing")))

; `main` declares the IO its `extern` call performs. Without the tag it
; is AX3042 first, and this probe measures nothing about grounding:
; the gate asserts the refusal is AX4004 SPECIFICALLY, so any earlier
; error makes it fail for the wrong reason.
(pub :: main Int)
;@axiom:effect(io)
(pub fn (main) (noSuchThing 1))
